-- title:
--   Rescaling crossing coordinates by a unit and its inverse
-- statement:
--   Let $\hat{\mathcal O}$ be a commutative local ring and $\pi \in \hat{\mathcal O}$ an element that is not a unit. Write $R = \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,\hat{\mathcal O}\,\pi$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $\hat{\mathcal O}[[X_0, X_1]]$ (formal multivariate power series in the index type $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$) by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - \pi$, and let $U\,\pi$ and $V\,\pi$ denote the classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$ in $R$. The assertion is that for every unit $\gamma \in R^\times$ there exists an $\hat{\mathcal O}$-algebra isomorphism $\tau : R \simeq R$ with $\tau(U\,\pi) = \gamma \cdot U\,\pi$ and $\tau(V\,\pi) = \gamma^{-1} \cdot V\,\pi$, where $\gamma$ and $\gamma^{-1}$ are taken as elements of $R$ via the coercion from the unit group. Thus $(\gamma\, U\,\pi, \gamma^{-1} V\,\pi)$ is again a pair of crossing coordinates for the same ring, the pair being exchanged with $(U\,\pi, V\,\pi)$ by an automorphism of $R$ over $\hat{\mathcal O}$.
--
--   The statement supplies the rescaling automorphisms of the local crossing model $\hat{\mathcal O}[[u,v]]/(uv - \pi)$, which allow a pair of coordinates of the form $(\gamma u, \gamma^{-1} v)$ to be normalised to $(u,v)$. It is used in the analysis of automorphisms of the crossing model and their fixed rings, in particular by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_algHom_range_eq_fixedPoints_apply_U_apply_V_of_tangent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_algHom_range_eq_fixedPoints_apply_U_apply_V_of_tangent).
